# SHA-256 integrity hash for config/allowlist.json
#
# The orchestrator's verify_allowlist() function computes the SHA-256 digest
# of allowlist.json at runtime and compares it against the expected hash below.
# If the hashes do not match, execution is refused (AllowlistError raised).
#
# Mechanism:
#   1. Read the raw bytes of config/allowlist.json
#   2. Compute SHA-256 of those bytes
#   3. Compare the hex digest against the expected_hash parameter
#   4. Reject if mismatch (detects tampering or accidental edits)
#
# To regenerate after modifying allowlist.json:
#   shasum -a 256 config/allowlist.json | awk '{print $1}' > config/allowlist.sha256.tmp
#   # Then update the hash value below
#
# Expected hash (hex digest):
5ce98591570125a7f974c921a8373f407002e3e6a3bfa3a050db69824dea7ea7
